\title "Chord diagrams"
\track "Gtr I"
\ts (4 4)
\chord ("C" 0 1 0 2 3 x)
\chord ("Am" 0 1 2 2 0 x)
\chord ("F" 1 1 2 3 3 1)
\chord ("A" 5 5 6 7 7 5)
\chord ("G" 3 0 0 0 2 3)
(0.1 1.2 0.3 2.4 3.5).2{ch "C" txt "1. Under the title: the Chord chart, C Am F A G Em D once each, in plain ink. E and N.C. have no shape, so they are not in it"}
  (0.1 1.2 2.3 2.4 0.5).2{ch "Am"} |
(1.1 1.2 2.3 3.4 3.5 1.6).2{ch "F" txt "2. A small diagram under each chord name, the text over them. C and Am have a thick nut; the A in bar 3 says 5fr"}
  (0.1 1.2 0.3 2.4 3.5).2{ch "C"} |
(5.1 5.2 6.3 7.4 7.5 5.6).2{ch "A"} (3.1 0.2 0.3 0.4 2.5 3.6).2{ch "G"} |
(0.1 0.2 1.3 2.4 2.5 0.6).1{ch "E" txt "3. E has no shape here: its name only, no diagram"} |
(0.1 1.2 0.3 2.4 3.5).2{ch "C" txt "4. Every C has its diagram. Press the A diagram in bar 3: it and its name turn blue, with a dashed line to its notes. Double-click it: the Chords panel opens on A, ready to edit"}
  (0.1 1.2 0.3 2.4 3.5).2{ch "C"} |
(0.1 1.2 2.3 2.4 0.5).2{ch "Am" txt "5. View options (the eye over the clip), or Settings, Tab, Notation: turn Chord diagrams off, then Chord chart off; each goes. Turn both on again"}
  (1.1 1.2 2.3 3.4 3.5 1.6).2{ch "F"} |
(3.1 0.2 0.3 0.4 2.5 3.6).2{ch "G" txt "6. Export: the PNG and SVG previews show the chart and the diagrams too"}
  (0.1 1.2 0.3 2.4 3.5).2{ch "C"} |
r.1{ch "N.C." txt "7. Pick Gtr II in Track: the chart is the same, every track's chords together"} |
\track "Gtr II"
\chord ("Em" 0 0 0 2 2 0)
\chord ("C" 0 1 0 2 3 x)
\chord ("D" 2 3 2 0 x x)
r.1 | r.1 | r.1 | (0.1 0.2 0.3 2.4 2.5 0.6).1{ch "Em"} |
(0.1 1.2 0.3 2.4 3.5).1{ch "C"} | (2.1 3.2 2.3 0.4).1{ch "D"} | r.1 | r.1 |

